<!DOCTYPE suite SYSTEM "https://testng.org/testng-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Atomberg – SHARE FLOW PROBE  (capture run, no assertions)
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Walks the ADMIN's long-press share journey and dumps a screenshot + page
  source at every step:

      probe_01_home                 the Devices dashboard
      probe_02_longpress_menu       the long-press context menu
      probe_03_after_share_device   what "Share device" opens
      probe_04_after_family_dialog  after the "Share access to family?" Yes
      probe_05_custom_toggles       the Custom capability toggles, if a picker exists

  Run this FIRST after installing the permission-levels (Super/Basic/Custom) APK.
  The log answers the two questions that decide the shape of the matrix work:

      1. Does a Super/Basic/Custom picker appear, and at which step?
      2. Is the family-wide confirmation dialog still there? If it is, sharing is
         still per-FAMILY and a per-device matrix stays meaningless. If it is gone,
         sharing is per-DEVICE and the SharedAccess matrix becomes real again.

  ── Run ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      mvn test "-DsuiteFile=testng-probe.xml"

  Both phones must be connected and pre-logged-in (the member phone is not
  driven, but BaseDeviceSharingTest still opens both sessions). Nothing is
  asserted and nothing is cleaned up: an invite code is generated that nobody
  redeems, and it expires on its own.
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-->
<suite name="Atomberg – Share Flow Probe" verbose="2">

    <test name="Probe – long-press share journey">
        <classes>
            <class name="com.appTest.tests.ShareFlowProbeTest"/>
        </classes>
    </test>

</suite>
